"""Atlas content for patch 7.0, part 2: MSQ #891 The Leap to Yak T'el to #920 All Aboard. Arc tag zc. Data only
(docs/atlas/era-modules.md is the contract).

Researched 2026-11-19 from the saved Console Games Wiki wikitext (lanes D06-D10); every locator is an exact substring of
a quest's Journal, Steps or main dialogue (stage directions and duty dialogue included, never optional pop-ups or
choice branches). Spoiler rules this module follows:
  - the Dawntrail cast that part 1 introduces earlier (Zoraal Ja, Bakool Ja Ja, Sareel Ja, Ketenramm, Cahciua, Namikka,
    the Xbr'aal, the Mamool Ja, Yak T'el) reuses the conventional ids; each first presentation here stands on its own as
    of its step, so this era lints alone;
  - the Vulture (#908) follows Marques -> Cid: char-vulture keeps its entry, and char-wihuwte gets a revealed-as edge
    from #909, where Zekowa names the Vulture as the Dustwatch's deputy chief, with "The Vulture" as his alias;
  - the voice beyond the golden city's gate (#905) and the woman watching the attack (#913) are named only in speaker
    labels and wiki links, so the text leaves them unnamed and no entity is made for them;
  - first names and titles only: "Galuf", never his surname; "Master Galuf" as Hunmu Rruk says it.
"""

def P(frm, until, scope, name, summary, claims, aliases=()):
    return dict(frm=frm, until=until, scope=scope, name=name, aliases=list(aliases), summary=summary, claims=claims)

