DECISIONS = [
 "**Five arcs (zc1–zc5)** cover every step from #891 to #920 without sharing steps (7, 5, 4, 6 and 8 steps); none reuses a quest title.",
 "**Part 1's cast reuses conventional ids** (`char-zoraal-ja`, `char-bakool-ja-ja`, `char-sareel-ja`, `char-ketenramm`, `char-cahciua`, `char-namikka`, `org-xbraal`, `org-mamool-ja`, `loc-yak-tel`), each with a presentation from its first step here, so this era lints alone. If part 1 picks other ids, the lead should rename these.",
 "**Wuk Lamat's birth father** is a `child-of` edge to Hunmu Rruk from #895, where he tells you she is the daughter he gave to Gulool Ja Ja (M895g); #896's Journal makes it public (M896b). The accepted `child-of` edge to Gulool Ja Ja stays, as the father who raised her.",
 "**The Vulture follows Marques → Cid.** `char-vulture` is the alias at #908; from #909, where Zekowa names him the Dustwatch's deputy chief and Wihuwte holds the bracelet, a `revealed-as` edge points to `char-wihuwte`, who carries \"The Vulture\" as an alias. Wihuwte is named from #908 only: at #906 his speaker tag is \"Frustrated Gentleman\".",
 "**The throne changes hands at #904**: `ADJUST` ends the accepted `rel-gulool-ja-ja-leads-tuliyollal` there, and Wuk Lamat and Koana each get a `leads` edge. Gulool Ja Ja's death (#914) ends `rel-zoraal-ja-opposes-gulool-ja-ja` and `rel-ketenramm-allied-with-gulool-ja-ja`.",
 "**Gulool Ja Ja's two heads**: his dead head of Reason is told in his #904 presentation, not made an entity (unnamed on the page). His alias moves from \"The Dawnservant\" to \"The former Dawnservant\" at #904.",
 "**The voice beyond the gate (#905) and the woman watching the attack (#913)** are named only in speaker labels and wiki links, so the text calls them \"a voice\" or leaves them out, and no entity is made.",
 "**Left out as entities** (named in text only, or not at all): Wuk Evu, Mablu, Tobli, Peshekwa/Peshiwa, Gurfurlur, Zurmurwur (\"a Yok Huy\" at #919), Shepetto, Shenza, Zawpya, Kwikana, Liwine, the Dawnblazer, the Vanguard stronghold, Moxutural Zooj, the Ja Tiika Heartland, Sheshenewezi Springs, Hhusatahwi, Tonatenyawi, Mehwahhetsoan, the Hoobigo and Boonewa clans.",
 "**Surnames out:** Galuf's surname (#903, #915) appears only in locators.",
]

